      text: "She could not spare the time to win the argument outright, not with three customers waiting and the fog due within the hour, so she let him have the last clause and simply agreed to have her book ready by quarter-day. Fessup seemed satisfied with that, which told her rather more about his actual instructions than anything he had read aloud. He left the ribbon's mark pressed into her counter like a bruise. She had a quarter-day now, and a great deal to do in it.",
